= Programming with Rudiments using the inetsocketclient class =

The [../classes/html/classinetsocketclient.html inetsocketclient class] provides methods for connecting to servers over inet (TCP/IP) sockets.

Here's the code for a client that can communicate with the [inetsocketserver.html inetsocketserver program].  This client connects to a server, sends a string, reads what the server sends back, and prints it out.

The host, port, timeout, retry wait, and number of tries are all configurable.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@../../examples/inetsocketclient.cpp@
}}}
}}}

Inet sockets allow clients and servers to communicate across a network.  Unix sockets can be used to allow clients and servers on the same machine to communicate.  Though clients and servers on the same machine could communicate over an inet socket using localhost, unix sockets are much faster and use fewer system resources.  See the [unixsocketserver.html unixsocketserver] and [unixsocketclient.html unixsocketclient] examples.

